    "notes": "Object: Project Equinox SteerCo #4 recap - GY's draft Binding Offer (purchase price incl. earn-out, valuation reflected in the ECL, exclusivity from Keppel within one week as a BO condition, confirmatory DD appendix, W&I non-recourse) is due by 5pm SGT Monday, with issues-list points TEC-28 and T-08 open.\nAction: Get the draft BO to MCIF for inputs (Jeremiah's 'tonight' was Fri 18 Sep, so it is overdue unless sent), confirm whether TEC-28 comes off the issues list and whether T-08 is a price adjustment, and submit the BO by 5pm SGT.\nDeadline: Mon 21 Sep 2026\nRecommended: Treat T-08 as a price adjustment with a short, tax-focused indemnity list, make exclusivity a stated BO condition, and keep TEC-28 on the list until the technical or DD owner confirms it is resolved.\nOpen questions: 1) Was the draft BO already sent to MCIF on Friday night? 2) What are TEC-28 and T-08 about, and is TEC-28 resolved? 3) What is GY's position on the SHLs (GY keeps and novates vs MCIF wanting repayment before closing)? 4) What earn-out amount and total price go into the BO, and who drafts the ECL? 5) What refundable deposit will MCIF confirm, and are the two third-party debt repayment wordings ready?\nParticipants: Jeremiah Phoon, Rohan Singh, Pedro Parra, Shaun Lee (Finergreen); Jeb Victorino, Carol Tock, Jolyn Ang (Climate Fund Managers / MCIF); James Fisher (CMS); Sonya Kalnin, Chanchanok Poolvoralaks (WFW); F. Gluck (GreenYellow); Keppel (seller)\nCategory: M&A | Project Equinox\nDraft reply: in the Email Triage dashboard, item #4",
